 How to Install Linux to VirtualBox Heinonen 2026

Cyber Lab Setup: Using Linux in a virtual machine allows users to practice and test security tools safely, in a separate environment from the host machine.

Installation Pitfalls: VirtualBox's unattended installation will sometimes fail, but manual configuration using an attached ISO image will allow a reliable configuration. Using sufficient resources (RAM, CPU cores, dynamic virtual disk storage), and enabling hardware virtualization (VT-x) in the host BIOS is crucial.

